QuestGuidance.Register("en",304,{
[9697]="70015474\n1\tDefeat goblin guards in Durin's Way (total: 2)\030Defeat Captain Gomîg\tCaptain Gomîg and his guards can be found in the northern passages west of the Door to the Clouds. Hoping to clear the way to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, Siggir has asked you to defeat the captain of the goblins in western Durin's Way.\n2\tTalk to Siggir at the Door to the Clouds\tSiggir is at the Door to the Clouds. You should return to the Door to the Clouds and inform Siggir that you have defeated Captain Gomîg and his guards.\n",
[9698]="70037A71\n1\tReclaim stolen plunder from the half-orcs (total: 8)\tTreasure chests filled with stolen loot can be found in Fushum Raus. You should reclaim the treasure for the Rohirrim.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have reclaimed the stolen treasures amassed in Fushum Raus.\n",
[9699]="700266E2\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers in the Way of Kings (total: 12)\tTomb-robbers can be found within the Way of Kings. Nethrandir asked you to defeat tomb-robbers within the Way of Kings.\n2\tTalk to Nethrandir in the Way of Kings\tNethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nethrandir will be pleased to hear that many tomb-robbers have been defeated.\n",
[9700]="700270B5\n1\tCollect daggers (total: 3)\030Collect spears (total: 3)\030Collect shields (total: 3)\030Collect bows and arrows (total: 3)\tDaggers, bows, spears, and shields can be found on the various Dunlending-scouts who roam the northern fields of the Herd-lands in Trum Dreng. You should defeat the Dragon-clan invaders and collect their weapons to give to the small band of trapped Dunlendings.\n2\tBring the weapons you gathered to Ceri\tCeri can be found on the overlook to the north of the Herd-lands. You should bring the weapons you gathered to the small group of hiding Dunlendings, which will help them be better prepared for the troubles they will face upon their escape.\n",
[9701]="70019003\n1\tHunt the Hornéd Wood-lord for his antlers\tThe Hornéd Wood-lord roams the Golden Wood in an area called Egladil, in south-east Lothlórien. Asmund has asked you to undertake one last hunt: to claim the antlers of the Hornéd Wood-lord.\n2\tBring Wood-lord's antlers to Asmund\tAsmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lothlórien. You have hunted the Hornéd Wood-lord for his antlers and should bring them now to Asmund.\n",
[9702]="70019004\n1\tHunt protected boars in Lórien for boar meat (total: 6)\tProtected boars can be found within Lothlórien, in places called Eryn Laer and on the banks of the Anduin in Gelirdor. Asmund has asked you to hunt protected boars within Lothlórien.\n2\tBring protected boar meat to Asmund\tAsmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lothlórien. You have hunted the protected boars of Lothlórien and should return now with the meat to Asmund.\n",
[9703]="70019000\n1\tHunt protected deer in Lórien for deer meat (total: 6)\tProtected deer can be found in Lórien, wandering in Nan Celebrant and Gelirdor. Asmund has asked you to hunt the protected deer of Lórien, promising to reward you well for it.\n2\tBring protected deer meat to Asmund\tAsmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lórien. You have hunted some of the protected deer of Lórien for Asmund and should return now to him.\n",
[9704]="7002EF4C\n1\tFind the Orc that escaped with Utlac's prized arrow\tThe Orc on which Utlac wasted his prized arrow ran south of Mansig's camp, and the archer thinks that he may have followed the course of the streams as they flow out of and back into the East Wall. Utlac feels badly about wasting his prized red-fletched arrow and wants you to find the Orc that carried it away after the ambush.\n2\tBring the red-fletched arrow to Utlac\tUtlac is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall. You have recovered the red-fletched arrow that Utlac wanted you to find and should bring it back to him.\n",
[9705]="70032D94\n1\tDestroy brewing stations (total: 6)\tStoves used for brewing poisons can be found in Baiúrz-mur. You should destroy the defilers' stoves as you encounter them in this Orc-infested passage of Zelem-melek.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many of the stoves used for poison-craft in Baiúrz-mur. With luck, the Orcs will not have the resources to rebuild their potion-crafting hall.\n",
[9706]="7000E8B5\n1\tDefeat the Tarkrîp Defiler\tNan Wathren lies to the north-east of Trestlebridge in the North Downs, far to the north of Bree. Nidgyl has asked you to slay the Tarkrîp Defiler who has been creating the poisons used by the Orcs attacking Trestlebridge.\n2\tTalk to Nidgyl\tNidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the south of Nan Wathren and Trestlebridge. You should return to Nidgyl and tell him that the Tarkrîp Defiler is dead.\n",
[9707]="7005978B\n1\tPoisoned critters can be found in the Wildwood. You should cure the poisoned critters.\t\n2\tCompleted\tCured poisoned critters in the Wildwood.\n",
[9708]="70025B2C\n1\tUse the Concoction on the Ivy (total: 8)\tTham Nambarth is east of Tinnudir. Gúrhebnir asked you to go to Tham Nambarth and apply his concoction to the ivy you find there.\n2\tSpeak to Gúrhebnir\tGúrhebnir is at Tinnudir, west of Tham Nambarth. Gúrhebnir will be discouraged to hear his concoction did nothing immediately.\n",
[9709]="70032D82\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Baiúrz-mur\tOrc-defilers and their masters can be found in Baiúrz-mur in Zelem-melek. You should defeat the Orc-defilers and the masterminds of the initiative to poison the enemies of evil.\n2\tDefeat defilers at Baiúrz-mur (total: 8)\030Defeat Orc leaders at Baiúrz-mur (total: 2)\tOrc-defilers and their masters can be found in Baiúrz-mur in Zelem-melek. You should defeat the Orc-defilers and the masterminds of the initiative to poison the enemies of evil.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Orc-poisoners and their masters, halting their evident plot to spread their crafted poisons beyond these walls.\n",
[9710]="700087B6\n1\tPoison the Hoardale River\tThe source of the Hoardale is at the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen. Uglash sent you to poison the enemy's water source.\n2\tReturn to Uglash at Gramsfoot\tUglash awaits your return at Gramsfoot. You climbed to the top of the falls and poisoned the waters of the Hoardale. You should return to Uglash with the news.\n",
[9711]="7002BFAF\n1\tCollect venom-sacs (total: 10)\tInsects may be found at the Creeping Mud to the north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Gisalic has asked you to collect venom sacs from the insects of the Rushgore.\n2\tTalk to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tGisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the Creeping Mud. You should bring the venom-sacs you collected to Gisalic at once.\n",
[9712]="70053E32\n1\tBurn noisome fungus (total: 12)\030Destroy poison mushrooms (total: 4)\tNoisome fungus and poison mushrooms can be found in Rath Dúath. You should burn noisome fungus and destroy poison mushrooms in Rath Dúath.\n2\tCompleted\tBurned noisome fungus and destroyed poison mushrooms in Rath Dúath.\n",
[9713]="7006BF4B\n1\tDestroy the Barkhûshim siege weapons (total: 6)\tMizâdi has asked you to sneak into Kûr Anzar and sabotage the Barkhûshim siege weapons intended for use in an assault on Urmâkh. Kûr Anzar can be found due east of Urmâkh.\n2\tReturn to Mizâdi in Urmâkh\tReturn to Mizâdi in Urmâkh with the good news.\n",
[9714]="7002AAB1\n1\tCatch the list of lost goods that Goldie dropped\030Catch Goldie's lost spectacles\030Catch Goldie's lost chair\030Catch Goldie's lost hat\030Catch Goldie's lost tea-cup\tGoldie Tunnelly's lost goods have been dropped into the Fishing Hole in Bywater. She suspects that the pond robbed her. You should try to fish up Goldie's lost goods so that she abandons her strange notion that she has been robbed by a small body of water.\n2\tBring Goldie the goods she dropped into the pond\tGoldie Tunnelly is near the Pond in Bywater. You should return to Goldie Tunnelly and give her all the goods you wrangled fromt he Pond.\n",
[9715]="7002CB80\n1\tSearch for a deep vein of copper ore\tBrid wants you to finish the mission of his prospectors. You should search for a deep copper vein in the Limlight Gorge to help complete Brid's map. Beware of bands of marauding trolls that might be attracted by the sound of your mining.\n2\tSearch for a deep vein of copper ore\tBrid wants you to finish the mission of his prospectors. You should search for a deep copper vein in the Limlight Gorge to help complete Brid's map. Beware of bands of marauding trolls that might be attracted by the sound of your mining.\n3\tSearch for a deep vein of iron ore\tYou should seek out a deep vein of iron ore to help complete Brid's map. The trolls seem to have been angered by your activities, so be on guard.\n4\tSearch for a deep vein of iron ore\tYou should seek out a deep vein of iron ore to help complete Brid's map. The trolls seem to have been angered by your activities, so be on guard.\n5\tSearch for a deep vein of silver ore\tYou should seek out a deep vein of silver ore to help complete Brid's map. The trolls are infuriated and likely to attack in great force should you continue.\n6\tSearch for a deep vein of silver ore\tYou should seek out a deep vein of silver ore to help complete Brid's map. The trolls are infuriated and likely to attack in great force should you continue.\n7\tTalk to Brid\tYou should let Brid know that you have discovered all three veins of ore, completed the prospector's map, and driven off many of the trolls in the area.\n",
[9716]="7002CB7E\n1\tDefeat Ghâmp\tYou must defeat the giant troll Ghâmp in his lair east of the prospector's shack and search for Witmund's remains.\n2\tSearch for Witmund's remains\tYou should search Ghâmp's lair for Witmund's remains.\n3\tDefeat Gank\tHaving defeated Ghâmp, you must now defeat Gank in his lair, west of the prospector's shack and search for Gyrth's remains.\n4\tSearch for Gyrth's remains\tYou should search Gank's lair for Gyrth's remains.\n5\tBring Brid the remaining map-fragments\tHaving defeated the two great trolls and recovered the final segments of the map, you should return to the prospector's shack and speak with Brid.\n",
[9717]="7002CB7C\n1\tDefeat Marauding Stone-trolls (total: 3)\030Collect prospector's map-fragments (total: 3)\tBrid wants you to take vengeance upon the marauding trolls in the Limlight Gorge and recover the prospector's map.\n2\tBring the map pieces to Brid\tHaving defeated a number of trolls and gathered several pieces of the map, you should return them to Brid at the prospector's shack.\n",
[9718]="700079A3\n1\tTalk to Filbert Burrows\tFilbert Burrows should be somewhere along the road east of Combe heading towards the Chetwood. Posco Burrows has asked you to look for his uncle, Filbert, and make sure he is unharmed.\n2\tCollect Filbert's Handkerchief\tCole Sickleleaf is at the ruins between the main Blackwold encampment and Skunkwood's Farm. You found Posco Burrow's uncle, Filbert, sitting on a stump at the cross-roads in the Chetwood. He wants you to collect a handkerchief taken by Cole Sickleleaf.\n3\tBring the handkerchief to Filbert Burrows\030Collect Filbert's handkerchief\tFilbert Burrows is waiting at the cross-roads in the Chetwood. You should return Filbert Burrow's handkerchief to him and convince him to leave the area.\n4\tTalk to Posco Burrows\tPosco Burrows is waiting for you at the Lumber Camp by Combe. Filbert Burrows, determined to remain where he is until the Blackwolds relent, has asked you to return to Combe to tell his nephew, Posco Burrows, that he is fine.\n",
[9719]="7002F977\n1\tPost warnings along the road (total: 4)\tPosts for hanging signage can be found along many of the roads and farms across the plains south and east of Cliving. Athelward has asked you to post warning signs along any posts by the roadsides and fields.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward resides in his Mead Hall at the eastern edge of Cliving. Athelward will be pleased to hear that you have placed suitable warnings along the roads outside Cliving.\n",
[9720]="70061389\n1\tFind the stolen potatoes in Ost Lagorath\tElgar Crowfoot is holed up in Ost Lagorath to the north-east. You should find the stolen potatoes there.\n2\tTake the stolen potatoes and defeat Elgar Crowfoot\tIf you defeat Elgar Crowfoot, the rest of the ruffians won't return to threaten Gamwich. You should steal back the stolen potatoes to lure him out.\n3\tTalk to Adro\tYou have defeated Elgar Crowfoot and reclaimed the stolen potatoes. You should return to Adro outside of Gamwich.\n",
[9721]="7006138F\n1\tImbert has asked you to solve the mystery of why his potatoes are sprouting. You should examine the potato sacks in his yard.\t\n2\tCheck one last sack\tThe potatoes in the first two sacks you checked haven't sprouted at all. Maybe you should check one last potato sack....\n3\tFollow the potato trail\tOne of Imbert's potato sacks is indeed filled with sprouted potatoes. You also found a trail of potatoes leading away from Imbert's house. You should follow the trail.\n4\tTalk to Adro\tThe potato trail ends right at the feet of a hobbit waiting outside Gamwich. You should question this suspicious hobbit.\n",
[9722]="7002618F\n1\tCollect Gauradan-pouches (total: 4)\tGauradan-pouches can be found at their camp in the Even-rills, north-east of the Eavespires. Remmenylf asked you to bring him several of the pouches the Gauredain have in their camp.\n2\tBring the Gauradan pouches to Remmenylf at the Eavespires\tRemmenylf can be found at the Eavespires, south-west of the Even-rills. Remmenylf will want to examine the Gauradan shaman pouches you recovered.\n",
[9723]="700377B3\n1\tDefeat all waves of bombers and their leaders\tStop the Orc bombers from destroying the gate-house. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9724]="7003A4A2\n1\tDefeat Orc-sappers behind the gate (total: 30)\030Defeat the Uruk-hai commander\tThe Orc and Uruk-hai attackers have brought black powder to the central gate of Helm's dike. They must be stopped before they are able to destroy the barricades and weaken the central gate. The Rohirrim are focused on defending the trenches and will rely on you to stop the flanking infiltrators. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9725]="7006AE97\n1\tDestroy vile effigies (total: 3)\tA powerful creature stalks the halls of Ghâr Mejet. Destroy vile effigies in the area and then confront the creature.\n2\tDefeat Lâkhmar\tConfront Lâkhmar and drive the foul creature away.\n3\tTalk to Yâshri\tTalk to Yâshri and inform her that the creature has been felled. Yâshri can be found just north of Ghâr Mejet.\n",
[9726]="700260C7\n1\tThe Masters and Mistresses of Apprentices would like to see you rewarded for your efforts. Speak with [see journal] in the crafting area.\t\n",
[9727]="70026793\n1\tThe Masters and Mistresses of Apprentices would like to see you rewarded for your efforts. Speak with [see journal] in the crafting area.\t\n",
